; ==============================================================================
; 1. Delegation Surface Mapping (read-only until task-7 lands)
; ==============================================================================

; --- 1.1. kernel.t27 actor tree (node ids, lane children) -----------------------------------
; 
;   Tree data: node 0 (root), node 1 (queen), node 2 (lanes supervisor), 
;   node 3 (services supervisor), nodes 4-8 (services), nodes 9+ (lanes).
;   Lanes are TRANSIENT, others PERMANENT; restart: one_for_one at all levels.
;   Lane parent: N_LANES (node 2); service parent: N_SERVICES (node 3).
;   Lane exits: KD_NOTHING (normal end), KD_RESTART (crash, within MaxR), 
;   KD_OWNER_REQUEST (crash, MaxR exceeded) — see lane_decision in kernel.t27.
;
;   Engine touchpoint: kernel.t27 node data, lane spawn paths.
;

; --- 1.2. specs/queen/actors.t27 sync-call infrastructure ---------------------------------
;
;   Call model: depth-limited (CALL_MAX_DEPTH=8), chain tracing (64 slots),
;   reply via alias (M_TASK_OFFER is a message tag). 
;   Message tags: M_TASK_OFFER=1 (task offer), M_RESULT (to be added).
;   Call states: CALL_PENDING, CALL_REPLY, CALL_DOWN, CALL_TIMEOUT, CALL_CYCLE, CALL_TOO_DEEP.
;   Child exit reasons tracked via monitors: DOWN messages.
;   Sync call: caller blocks with `after`, callee replies to alias, caller deactivates alias and demonitors.
;
;   Engine touchpoints: extend with M_RESULT, call tracing for delegation chain, 
;   depth budget checks (engine scope vs CALL_MAX_DEPTH).
;

; --- 1.3. dispatch.t27/claim.t27 lease/retry/escalation -----------------------------------
;
;   Lease system: queen_lease table (TTL 180s, heartbeat 60s), one Queen at a time.
;   Task dispatch state: S_QUEUED → S_RUNNING → S_ACCEPTED/REJECTED/ESCALATED/ENDED.
;   Retry policy: 2 send-backs then escalate (SENDBACK_CEILING=2), 
;   MAX_CEILING_RELEASES=1 (retry ceiling).
;   Escalation: reviewed by queend based on criteria, can accept, escalate, or send back.
;   Claim state: C_OFFER → C_ACCEPTED/REJECTED/FAILED, with lease/capacity rules.
;
;   Engine touchpoints: integrate with review_valve.t27 escalation_kind, 
;   interpret review verdicts as delegation decisions, integrate lease for engine heartbeat.
;

; --- 1.4. term_pane.t27 + pty_server.t27 pane spawn path -----------------------------------
;
;   Pane lifecycle: term_pane.t27 manages grid/keyboard display, pty_server.t27 spawns processes.
;   Spawn path: pty_server.t27 uses sys_forkpty/sys_execv or client_spawn,
;   per agent (agent id in pty_client.t27), persistent across window reopen.
;   Agent model: AGENT 0 = Claude Code, spawns model-specific processes.
;   Spawn plan: R_RESUME (existing pane), R_RELAUNCH (new key/model).
;   Pane state: offline, starting, running, respawn logic on key change.
;
;   Engine touchpoints: spawn child delegates with explicit budget, wrap spawned processes 
;   for cancellation/history restart, integrate pane lifecycle with engine scope.
;

; ==============================================================================
; 2. Engine Design Skeleton (to be implemented after task-7 lands)
